  "ai_language_tip": "Use polite standard Italian (it) with 'Lei'; English works in major tourist areas and hotels but much less at clinics, trades and small towns; regional accents are strong but everyone understands standard Italian.",
  "english_ok": "sometimes — Good in hotels and tourist restaurants in Rome, Florence, Venice, Milan; limited in clinics, garages, CUP lines and small towns.",
  "politeness": "Formal 'Lei'; open with 'Buongiorno' (until mid-afternoon) or 'Buonasera'; titles matter ('Dottore/Dottoressa' for doctors and graduates, 'Signor/Signora'); close with 'Grazie, arrivederci'.",
  "name_tip": "Bookings 'a nome di …' (surname); spell with the Italian city-name alphabet ('A come Ancona, B come Bologna'); foreign names should be spelled letter by letter.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile 3XX then 6–7 digits (e.g. 333 12345678), landlines start with 0 which must always be dialled (Rome 06, Milan 02); international +39 (San Marino +378, Vatican numbers sit inside the Rome 06 range); WhatsApp is very common.",
  "time_tip": "24h used in writing and often in speech ('alle 20'); 'le sette e mezza' = 7:30 (half past, no trap); 'otto meno un quarto' = 7:45; confirm 'di sera' or 'di mattina' when 12h is used.",
  "number_tip": "Mobile numbers are read 3-3-4 or in pairs; numbers are often said digit by digit; prices said as 'euro e centesimi'.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid lunch break about 13:00–15:30 (many shops and offices close), restaurant service 12:30–14:30 and 20:00–22:00, and Sunday; August (especially around Ferragosto, 15 August) many small businesses close for holidays.",
  "closed_days": "Many restaurants have a weekly closing day (giorno di chiusura, often Monday); many shops close Sunday and some on Monday morning; holidays include 6 January, Easter Monday, 25 April, 1 May, 2 June, 15 August, 1 November, 8, 25 and 26 December, plus local patron-saint days.",
  "booking_channels": "TheFork and phone for restaurants (WhatsApp increasingly); CUP regional booking centres (phone, web, pharmacies) for public specialist visits with the GP's electronic prescription; private clinics by phone or MioDottore; Treatwell/Uala-type apps or phone for salons; Glovo, Deliveroo and Just Eat for delivery.",
  "voice_menu": "CUP regional numbers, ASL/hospitals, banks, telecoms (TIM, Vodafone, WindTre, Iliad), Poste Italiane and utilities use IVR; restaurants and small shops answer directly.",
  "callback_habits": "CUP sends SMS reminders; restaurants may confirm by call or WhatsApp; small businesses commonly reply on WhatsApp.",
